[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Petrov's Defense"]
[Variation "Petrov's Defense: Classical Attack"]
[ECO "C42"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "centre-pawns,quick-development"]
[Kind "main"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 { The Petrov: Black attacks e4 instead of defending e5, hoping to trade pieces and reach a quiet, equal game. }
3. Nxe5 { Takes the pawn. Black cannot just grab e4 back: after ...Nxe4 the queen move Qe2 sets a trap, so Black first kicks this knight away. } 3... d6 (3... Nxe4 4. Qe2 Qe7 5. Qxe4 { Wins the knight for nothing: Black's queen cannot guard e4 through White's own knight on e5. ...d6 then hits the knight, so White retreats and stays a pawn up. } 5... d6 6. d4 dxe5 7. dxe5)
4. Nf3 { The knight retreats to its best square, central and ready to support d4. Black's d6 pawn was attacking it. } 4... Nxe4
5. d4 { Takes the centre and frees the c1 bishop. White has more space, and Black's knight on e4 has no easy way home. } 5... d5
6. Bd3 { Develops, eyes the knight on e4 and clears the way to castle. Black cannot easily trade it off. } 6... Be7 (6... Bd6 7. O-O O-O 8. c4 c6 9. Nc3 Nxc3 10. bxc3)
7. O-O { Castles before the centre opens, so the king is safe when lines open. } 7... Nc6 (7... Bg4 8. c4 Nc6 9. cxd5 Qxd5 10. Nc3) (7... O-O 8. c4 Nf6 9. Nc3 Nc6 10. Re1)
8. c4 { Hits the d5 pawn, which is what holds Black's knight on e4 in place. White is ahead in development, so opening the centre helps. } 8... Nb4
9. Be2 { Steps back before the knight on b4 can take the bishop. Trading it off would lose time and the bishop pair for nothing. } 9... O-O
10. Nc3 { Develops and attacks the knight on e4, which has to trade itself off. } 10... Bf5
11. a3 { Attacks the knight on b4, so it has to trade itself off. } 11... Nxc3 12. bxc3 { Recaptures towards the centre, so pawns on c3, c4 and d4 give White a strong grip. } 12... Nc6
{ Plan: finish development with Re1 and Bf4, and take on d5 with the c-pawn to open lines. If Black leaves the book, castle early and keep the pawns on c4 and d4 to hold the centre. } *
